    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d528">

                <pb facs="0811" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1946v05/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.6362/9–2446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Political Adviser for Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-24T21:00:00+02:00">September 24, 1946—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 26—9:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2245. Committee of Coal Experts having been again unable to reach agreement on
                    principles of allocation, 79th meeting of Coordinating Committee discussed
                    question further on September 23 (2119 and 2120 September 10). Discussion served
                    to clarify basic differences of opinion. While three western powers are willing
                    to agree to quadripartite allocation of all coal mined in Germany, Soviets
                    maintain that each zonal commander must first deduct needs of his occupying
                    forces and authorities following which balance of coal produced in his zone will
                    be available for quadripartite allocation. Soviets stated they are willing to
                    agree to quadripartite allocation of all coal produced only if there is also
                    quadripartite planning of coal production throughout Germany. Coordinating
                    Committee agrees to inform CFM of above after reporting to Control
                        Council.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d528-f1"/></p>
                <p>Repeat to Moscow as 282; Paris for Matthews as 299; London as 337.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Murphy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d528-f1" n="17" xml:id="d528-f1-content">
                <p>The Allied Control Council, at its 41st meeting, September 30, merely took note
                    of the failure of the Coordinating Committee to agree on coal allocations, the
                    report on which was being forwarded to the Council of Foreign Ministers. This
                    information was sent to the Department in telegram 2281, September 30, from
                    Berlin (740.00119 Control (Germany)/9–3046).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
